# CITATION metadata.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "EOV: Evolutionary Option Value is budget-stable but task-conditional"
abstract: >-
  Starting-point value in a fitness landscape is stable across search budgets,
  but transfers poorly across tasks. The degree of transfer is predictable from
  landscape similarity: Spearman rho = 0.744 in discovery and 0.754 in an
  independent confirmation (bootstrap 95% CI [0.232, 0.944]). About 16 shared
  genotype measurements suffice to decide whether an existing starting-point
  ranking is worth carrying into a new task. A zero-measurement gate built only
  from task metadata failed (NO-GO).
type: software
